WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:21.305
"That will be 25 cents, please," Henry said.

2
00:00:21.306 --> 00:00:23.937
He handed a cup of lemonade to Tiny.

3
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:27.759
Tiny was Henry's neighbor and the tallest kid in the tenth grade.

4
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.619
Tiny was also one of the lemonade stand's best customers.

5
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.160
He stopped by the stand to buy lemonade almost every day, sometimes more than once.

6
00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:42.933
"Here you go." Tiny handed over a few coins. "Thanks for the lemonade!"

7
00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:46.430
"You're welcome."

8
00:00:46.431 --> 00:00:49.735
After Tiny left, Henry looked at Cole.

9
00:00:49.736 --> 00:00:55.613
"I hope Maggie comes back soon," he said. "We're almost out of lemonade."

10
00:00:55.614 --> 00:01:00.967
Just then Nathan hurried over. "Hi, guys," said their friend.

11
00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:04.121
"How are the lemonade and detective businesses?"

12
00:01:04.122 --> 00:01:08.897
"Hi, Nathan," Henry said. "The lemonade business is great."

13
00:01:08.898 --> 00:01:14.431
"Yeah," Cole agreed. "But the detective business is a little slow."

14
00:01:14.432 --> 00:01:20.802
"It's a good thing we haven't been busy solving any mysteries this week, though," Henry reminded Cole.

15
00:01:20.803 --> 00:01:24.961
"Otherwise we wouldn't have had enough time to work on our float."

16
00:01:24.962 --> 00:01:30.388
Nathan looked interested. "A float? You mean for the parade?"

17
00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.843
Henry nodded.

18
00:01:31.844 --> 00:01:36.298
Belltown's annual Summer Parade was coming up that Saturday afternoon.

19
00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:39.907
Anyone in town could sign up to enter a float.

20
00:01:39.908 --> 00:01:43.724
"It's going to be awesome!" Cole told Nathan.

21
00:01:43.725 --> 00:01:47.626
"This is the first time The Lemonade Detectives are entering."

22
00:01:47.627 --> 00:01:54.171
Henry laughed. "It would have been hard for The Lemonade Detectives to enter a float last year.

23
00:01:54.172 --> 00:01:57.019
Our business didn't exist then!"

24
00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.628
"Good point." Cole grinned.

25
00:01:59.629 --> 00:02:04.168
"Anyway, we're sure to win the grand prize for Best Float."

26
00:02:04.169 --> 00:02:07.721
"That's what Maggie is hoping," Henry said.

27
00:02:07.722 --> 00:02:15.543
"She really wants that cash prize, especially since she spent all her money on that horse show last week."

28
00:02:15.544 --> 00:02:19.861
Cole pointed. "Speaking of Maggie, here she comes."

29
00:02:19.862 --> 00:02:26.547
Maggie was rushing toward them. She was clutching a pitcher of lemonade and a laptop computer.

30
00:02:26.548 --> 00:02:30.858
"You guys will never believe what I just found out!" she exclaimed.

31
00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:35.198
"There are going to be two prizes awarded at the parade this year!"

32
00:02:35.199 --> 00:02:42.368
"Two prizes?" Henry said. "Do you mean there's a first prize and a second prize?"

33
00:02:42.369 --> 00:02:47.298
"No, there will be two first prizes," Maggie said.

34
00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:53.071
"Huh?" Cole looked confused. "How can there be two first prizes?"

35
00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:58.219
Maggie looked impatient. "I'm trying to tell you," she said.

36
00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:03.791
"The mayor will award a cash prize for the best float, just like he does every year.

37
00:03:03.792 --> 00:03:07.394
But there's also going to be a poll on the town website.

38
00:03:07.395 --> 00:03:11.521
Anyone in town can vote for his or her favorite float."

39
00:03:11.522 --> 00:03:14.185
"Wow, cool!" Nathan said.

40
00:03:14.186 --> 00:03:18.214
"Does the winner of the popular vote get a cash prize too?"

41
00:03:18.215 --> 00:03:20.237
"No," Maggie said.

42
00:03:20.238 --> 00:03:24.573
"But the popular vote winner gets to be interviewed on TV."

43
00:03:24.574 --> 00:03:27.112
"That could be fun," Cole said.

44
00:03:27.113 --> 00:03:30.925
"Not just fun," Maggie said.

45
00:03:30.926 --> 00:03:36.609
"It would be great publicity for both of my—I mean our—businesses."

46
00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:43.894
She waved a hand at the signs advertising the lemonade stand and the detective business.

47
00:03:43.895 --> 00:03:47.822
Henry grabbed the laptop and opened it.

48
00:03:47.823 --> 00:03:50.219
The screen showed Belltown's website.

49
00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:54.641
"It looks like the popular poll isn't open yet," he said.

50
00:03:54.642 --> 00:03:57.993
"Of course it's not, silly." Maggie shrugged.

51
00:03:57.994 --> 00:04:02.607
"Nobody has seen any of the floats yet. They're all top secret."

52
00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:04.978
Henry scanned the website.

53
00:04:04.979 --> 00:04:10.455
"It says voting will start as soon as the parade is over on Saturday."

54
00:04:10.456 --> 00:04:12.947
Cole looked over Henry's shoulder.

55
00:04:12.948 --> 00:04:17.988
"What's that?" he asked, pointing to something at the bottom of the computer screen.

56
00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:21.171
Henry scrolled down for a better look.

57
00:04:21.172 --> 00:04:24.912
"It's a place where people can write comments about the parade.

58
00:04:24.913 --> 00:04:28.079
See? Here's a note from Mrs. Sweet."

59
00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.103
"It says, 'My float will be the sweetest treat in town,'" Maggie read.

60
00:04:33.104 --> 00:04:38.768
"Here's one from Miss Bishop, the lady who owns the jewelry store right across from the Sweet Shop."

61
00:04:38.769 --> 00:04:41.776
Cole leaned closer to read the comment.

62
00:04:41.777 --> 00:04:46.321
"She says, 'My float will win the gold medal for sure.'"

63
00:04:46.322 --> 00:04:51.858
Maggie snorted. "Those ladies can keep dreaming," she said.

64
00:04:51.859 --> 00:04:56.673
"The Lemonade Detectives are definitely going to win both of those prizes!"

65
00:04:56.674 --> 00:05:02.315
"I'll vote for you guys," Nathan promised. "What does your float look like?"

66
00:05:02.316 --> 00:05:06.732
Henry opened his mouth to answer, but Maggie spoke first.

67
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:11.557
"We can't tell you," she said to Nathan. "It's top secret."

68
00:05:11.558 --> 00:05:17.221
"Don't be silly, Maggie!" Cole laughed. "We can trust Nathan."

69
00:05:17.222 --> 00:05:21.954
Maggie looked uncertain. "Do you promise not to tell anyone?

70
00:05:21.955 --> 00:05:26.435
Especially your little sister, Nora. She has a big mouth."

71
00:05:26.436 --> 00:05:29.298
"I promise," Nathan said.

72
00:05:29.299 --> 00:05:35.705
"My sister is staying with my grandparents this week, so I couldn't tell her even if I wanted to."

73
00:05:35.706 --> 00:05:39.307
"Our float is really cool," Cole told him.

74
00:05:39.308 --> 00:05:45.869
"We made a huge lemon out of papier-mâché, and we're dressing it up to look like Sherlock Holmes."

75
00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.817
"Get it?" Henry said. "Sherlock Holmes is a famous detective.

76
00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:53.958
And we're The Lemonade Detectives."

77
00:05:53.959 --> 00:06:00.852
Nathan was laughing. "A lemon dressed like Sherlock Holmes? That's funny!"

78
00:06:00.853 --> 00:06:06.606
Suddenly Maggie spun around. "Hey!" she cried, pointing at a figure.

79
00:06:06.607 --> 00:06:11.846
"Who are you? Are you spying on us?"
